{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 35,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A Psalm",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of David. Plead ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my cause",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", O LORD, with them that strive with me: fight against them that fight against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take hold of shield and buckler, and stand up for my help.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Draw out also the spear, and stop ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the way",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against them that persecute me: say to my soul, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy salvation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them be confounded and put to shame that seek after my soul: let them be turned back and brought to confusion that devise my hurt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them be as chaff before the wind: and let the angel of the LORD chase ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let their way be dark and slippery: and let the angel of the LORD persecute them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For without cause they have hid for me their net ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a pit, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " without cause they have digged for my soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let destruction come upon him at unawares; and let his net that he hath hid catch himself: into that very destruction let him fall.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And my soul shall be joyful in the LORD: it shall rejoice in his salvation.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All my bones shall say, LORD, who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like thee, who deliverest the poor from him that is too strong for him, even the poor and the needy from him that spoileth him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "False witnesses arose; they laid to my charge ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that I knew not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They rewarded me evil for good ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the spoiling of my soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But as for me, when they were sick, my clothing ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sackcloth: I humbled my soul with fasting; and my prayer returned into my own bosom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I behaved myself as though ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he had been",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my friend ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "or",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brother: I bowed down heavily, as one that mourneth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mother.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But in my adversity they rejoiced, and assembled themselves: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yes",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the abjects assembled themselves against me, and I knew ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not; they did tear ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and ceased not:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With hypocritical mockers in feasts, they gnashed upon me with their teeth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "LORD, how long wilt thou look on? rescue my soul from their destructions, my darling from the lions.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will give thee thanks in the great congregation: I will praise thee among many people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let not them that are my enemies wrongfully rejoice over me: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "neither",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " let them wink with the eye that hate me without a cause.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they speak not peace: but they devise deceitful matters against ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them that are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " quiet in the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, they opened their mouth wide against me, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " said, Aha, aha, our eye hath seen ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou hast seen, O LORD: keep not silence: O LORD, be not far from me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Stir up thyself, and awake to my judgment, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to my cause, my God and my LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Judge me, O LORD my God, according to thy righteousness; and let them not rejoice over me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them not say in their hearts, Ah, so would we have it: let them not say, We have swallowed him up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them be ashamed and brought to confusion together that rejoice at my hurt: let them be clothed with shame and dishonor that magnify ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "themselves",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them shout for joy, and be glad, that favor my righteous cause: yes, let them say continually, Let the LORD be magnified, who hath pleasure in the prosperity of his servant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.35.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.35.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And my tongue shall speak of thy righteousness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of thy praise all the day long.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
